# Run 2026-10-31, boot A1 (superflat): SQ-EFX effect changes (queue section "SQ-EFX effect changes, 2026-10-31",
# added by the effects session at 00:44) and the D&D wood removal (SQ-RW-28). Runs after a1_data, before a1_world.
# Toml set before the A1 boot: [copper_poisoning] intervalSeconds = 10, jitterSeconds = 0, chancePerPiece = 1.0.
# Jars: patcherMod 1.1.04 of 10-31 00:44, creative_delight 00:29, backportedVinery -06 of 00:41, backportedBrewin -04.
# Needs spawn-animals=true (vanilla discards animals every tick otherwise): SQ-EFX-04 runs at A2.
# Bot "qe" (survival) takes the effects; ActiveEffects lists modded effects by "forge:id", vanilla ones by Id
# (Poison 19, Wither 20, Regeneration 10, Resistance 11, Fire Resistance 12, Absorption 22, Health Boost 21).
pace 2

## SQ-EFX-01 | effect mixins apply
bootreject (Mixin apply failed|InvalidInjectionException).*(CopperPoisoningEffectMixin|LivingEntityEffectRemapMixin|FruitsDelightEffectFuncMixin|CaffeinatedEffectMixin|LivingEntityUseItemIconMixin|CreateTeaPipeIconMixin|MobEffectTickContextMixin)
bootreject (?i)removeByPotion.*(error|fail)
bootreject Ignoring invalid wine effect entry
bootexpect \[(CE )?potions\]

## SQ-EFX-02 | Magic Resistance I stops Poison I
# perfBot bots are invulnerable (Bots.java setInvulnerable): damage reads use a NoAI pillager "qp" on Normal
# (zombies are undead: no Poison). Pillager max health 24.
> difficulty normal
> kill @e[type=minecraft:pillager]
> summon minecraft:pillager -46 -60 -46 {NoAI:1b,PersistenceRequired:1b,Tags:["qp"]}
sleep 1
> effect give @e[tag=qp,limit=1] creativeengineering:magic_resistance 60 0
> effect give @e[tag=qp,limit=1] minecraft:poison 10 0
> data get entity @e[tag=qp,limit=1] Health
sleep 6
> data get entity @e[tag=qp,limit=1] Health
look the two Health reads are equal (24.0f)
> effect clear @e[tag=qp,limit=1]

