> effect clear @e[tag=qp,limit=1]

## SQ-EFX-04 | Dragon Horse Armor: Regeneration II, Health Boost II, Resistance II
> summon minecraft:horse -46 -60 -50 {Tame:1b}
> item replace entity @e[type=minecraft:horse,limit=1,sort=nearest] horse.armor with dragonloot:dragon_horse_armor
sleep 10
> data get entity @e[type=minecraft:horse,limit=1] ActiveEffects
> data get entity @e[type=minecraft:horse,limit=1] Health
sleep 6
> data get entity @e[type=minecraft:horse,limit=1] Health
expect Id: 10, Amplifier: 1b
expect Id: 21, Amplifier: 1b
expect Id: 11, Amplifier: 1b
look Ids 10, 21 and 11 at Amplifier 1b; the second Health read not lower than the first (no drop at the 5 s refresh)
> kill @e[type=minecraft:horse]

## SQ-EFX-05 | Agility -> Climbing, Resilience -> Knockback Resistance, Chorus -> Teleport
> data get entity qe Pos
> effect give qe neapolitan:agility 30 0
> effect give qe quark:resilience 30 0
> effect give qe fruitsdelight:chorus 1 0
sleep 2
> data get entity qe ActiveEffects
> data get entity qe Pos
reject has the following entity data.*(neapolitan:agility|quark:resilience)
expect has the following entity data.*vinery:climbing_effect
expect has the following entity data.*alexsmobs:knockback_resistance
look the second Pos differs from the first (Teleport); an "Unknown effect" for agility or resilience means it is removed from the registry instead of remapped: read effects.md 2.7
> effect clear qe

